stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    lg0: Unmanaged
    lg1: Breaks NoRefusal or NoSilentLoss in some cases
    lg2: Path to the HomeFollowsDesignation or NoRefusal or NoSilentLoss bug
    lg3: Repeats forever, so HomeFollowsDesignation breaks
  }
  class lg0 tan
  class lg1 mayBreak
  class lg2 bugPath
  class lg3 repeats
  s0: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set)
  s1: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set), an input waits at the gateway
  s2: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node)
  s3: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway
  s4: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node) [refusal shown, 1 input lost]
  s5: No owner row, the gateway serves (no node set, designated node down), an input waits at the gateway
  s6: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway [refusal shown, 1 input lost]
  s7: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node) [refusal shown, 2 inputs lost]
  s8: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node), an input waits at the gateway [refusal shown, 2 inputs lost]
  s9: No owner row, the gateway serves (set to the designated node) [refusal shown, 3 inputs lost]
  [*] --> s0
  s0 --> s0: an operator edits one node's config file
  s0 --> s1: you send a message
  s0 --> s2: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s1 --> s1: an operator edits one node's config file
  s2 --> s3: you send a message
  s1 --> s5: the designated node stops
  s3 --> s4: the gateway refuses to place the channel on another node
  s5 --> s1: the designated node boots and ends its session of an older owner
  s1 --> s3: the hub copies its setting to the database
  s4 --> s6: you send a message
  s6 --> s7: the gateway refuses to place the channel on another node
  s7 --> s8: you send a message
  s8 --> s9: the gateway refuses to place the channel on another node
